From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wolfSSL <support@wolfssl.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ceph-volume: select FIPS-approved LUKS parameters for encrypted OSDs

ceph-volume calls "cryptsetup luksFormat" with neither --cipher nor --pbkdf,
so every encrypted OSD takes the LUKS2 defaults: aes-xts-plain64 for the
volume and argon2id for the keyslot. Neither is inside the wolfCrypt FIPS
module boundary, and argon2id is not served by wolfProvider at all, so an OSD
provisioned this way is encrypted with non-approved primitives while reporting
success.

Select the approved parameters in luks_format() so that "pveceph osd create
--encrypted" and "ceph-volume lvm create --dmcrypt" produce a conformant
header with no change at the call site:

  --cipher aes-cbc-essiv:sha256   bulk cipher and per-sector IV hash, served
                                  by the in-kernel wolfCrypt cbc(aes)
  --key-size 256                  AES-256. The upstream default of 512 sizes
                                  an XTS key, which has no meaning for CBC and
                                  is rejected outright
  --pbkdf pbkdf2 --hash sha256    keyslot KDF and hash, served by wolfProvider

Arguments supplied through --dmcrypt-format-opts are appended after these and
therefore still take precedence, so a caller may override any of them.

luks_open() is deliberately left unchanged. On an existing LUKS device the
volume key size is read from the header and cryptsetup ignores --key-size, so
the value it passes has no effect on the resulting mapping.

---
 src/ceph-volume/ceph_volume/util/encryption.py | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ceph-volume/ceph_volume/util/encryption.py b/src/ceph-volume/ceph_volume/util/encryption.py
--- a/src/ceph-volume/ceph_volume/util/encryption.py
+++ b/src/ceph-volume/ceph_volume/util/encryption.py
@@ -106,7 +106,10 @@
     base_cmd: List[str] = [
         'cryptsetup',
         '--batch-mode', # do not prompt
-        '--key-size', get_key_size_from_conf(),
+        '--cipher', 'aes-cbc-essiv:sha256',
+        '--key-size', '256',
+        '--pbkdf', 'pbkdf2',
+        '--hash', 'sha256',
         '--key-file', '-',
     ]

